# The keys trusted to sign commits and tags, read by .gitlab/ci/verify-signatures.sh from the
# protected branch. One per line: <email> namespaces="git" <key type> <public key>
# To rotate a key, keep the old line with valid-before="YYYYMMDD" and add the new key with
# valid-after="YYYYMMDD" (namespaces="git",valid-after="20270101"); each commit is checked
# against the key valid at its commit time, so history signed with the old key still verifies.
# The commit time is set by whoever signs, so dating a key out does not stop a stolen key from
# signing backdated commits: remove a compromised key's line instead, and re-sign what it signed.
